{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"23a4e24ed77988b274af93078277334f60572587a3ba1abda9b29874b6942675","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T02:47:55Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[99,102]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-live-binding.py","quoted_text":"DEPENDENCY_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<directive>Wants|Requires|Requisite|BindsTo|PartOf|Conflicts|\"\n    r\"WantedBy|RequiredBy|Also|Upholds|OnFailure|OnSuccess|Triggers|\"\n    r\"TriggersBy|Unit|Service)\\s*=\\s*(?P<value>.*)\")","reason":"DEPENDENCY_RE is the scan's list of [Unit] dependency directives that can affect the selected unit. It omits the systemd stop-propagation directives `PropagatesStopTo=` and its inverse `StopPropagatedFrom=`, so a co-installed unit that propagates stop to the selected service can be missed and `supported=True` reported incorrectly. This is an implementation gap in existing dependency detection, not a new requirement.","target":"f0738bf5042b39a7d78d66157d92718f35485bd0"},"finding_id":"1d6d3a879edaf2afe7e9a329fb5916c084c5d2f4f230f484983ff91ea4a44881","previous_event_id":"fa9679b72819522a409124ce274f9585d7ace8ad845b6af31f400cef3a61d093","review_id":"9a9770d007f4898ae9f169624c7b761856e1e349d118670986a85a8250d506cd"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:1d6d3a879edaf2afe7e9a329fb5916c084c5d2f4f230f484983ff91ea4a44881:52e9b1e796ce6b0b828fbdf8e6644ea195071fc3e53cf08f941373c756c9aa37"}